  "about": "Shared table for local runtime addresses (src-tauri/src/ai/local/endpoint.rs parse_loopback and the web-side mirror). After trimming whitespace at both ends exactly as JavaScript's String.prototype.trim does (U+FEFF is trimmed, U+0085 is not; Rust uses reasoning::js_trim), an address is accepted only when ALL hold: at most 200 characters, no space or control character; it starts with 'http://' (any case); the authority (text up to the first '/', '\\', '?' or '#') has no '@'; the host is written exactly '127.0.0.1', '[::1]' or 'localhost' (any case); an explicit port of 1 to 5 digits, no leading zero, value 1-65535; the rest is exactly '', '/', '/v1' or '/v1/'; a standard URL parser reads the same scheme, host and port and finds no user, query or fragment. 'base' is the normalised address: 'http://' + lower-case host + ':' + port, with no path.",
